---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Nav } from "../sections/Nav";
import Footer from "../sections/Footer.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | StenoAI"
  description="StenoAI privacy policy. Learn how we protect your data with local-first processing."
  canonical="https://stenoai.co/privacy/"
>
  <style>
    main.legal { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 24px 80px; }
    main.legal h1 {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: clamp(26px, 3.7vw, 37px);
      font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.035em; line-height: 1.1;
      color: var(--fg-1); margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .dateline { font-size: 13px; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 48px; }
    .content { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 32px; }
    .content section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
    main.legal h2 {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 17px; font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
      color: var(--fg-1);
    }
    main.legal h3 {
      font-family: var(--font-sans);
      font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500;
      color: var(--fg-1);
    }
    main.legal p { color: var(--fg-2); }
    main.legal strong { color: var(--fg-1); font-weight: 600; }
    main.legal ul { color: var(--fg-2); padding-left: 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
    main.legal a { text-decoration: underline; }
    main.legal code {
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 12px;
      background: var(--surface-hover);
      padding: 2px 6px;
      border-radius: 0;
      color: var(--fg-1);
    }
  </style>

  <Nav client:load />

  <main id="main-content" class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="dateline">Last updated: August 8, 2026</p>

    <div class="content">
      <section>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <p>StenoAI is a privacy-first, open-source meeting notes application that runs entirely on your local device. We are committed to protecting your privacy and being transparent about our data practices.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Data that stays on your device</h2>
        <p>The following data is processed and stored exclusively on your Mac and is never transmitted to any external server:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Audio recordings of your meetings</li>
          <li>Transcriptions generated by the local Whisper model</li>
          <li>AI-generated summaries, action items, and key points</li>
          <li>Session names, folders, and organizational data</li>
          <li>Optional numerical voice profiles used for speaker identification</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Speaker identification and voice profiles (optional)</h2>
        <p>Anonymous speaker separation within one meeting works independently of speaker identification. Cross-meeting speaker identification is off by default.</p>
        <p>If you enable speaker identification and create a named person, StenoAI derives a numerical biometric voice profile from excerpts you confirm. The profile is stored only on your device and is used to suggest that person in future meetings. Voice profiles and the audio used to create them are not sent to StenoAI or included in analytics.</p>
        <p>Speaker suggestions can be wrong and should be reviewed before you rely on them. You can delete a voice profile at any time in <strong>Settings &gt; People</strong>. Deleting a profile stops future matching and removes the person's stored profile, but it does not delete recordings or transcripts, which are managed separately.</p>
        <p>You are responsible for informing recorded people and establishing an appropriate legal basis for recording and creating a voice profile. StenoAI requires you to enable speaker identification in Settings before a named profile can be created, but StenoAI does not collect consent from the recorded person or record a separate authorization for each profile. Enabling the setting does not by itself establish legal compliance for your recording or use case.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Google Calendar integration (optional)</h2>
        <p>If you choose to connect Google Calendar, StenoAI accesses your calendar data with the <code>calendar.readonly</code> scope. This means:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>StenoAI can only <strong>read</strong> your calendar events; it cannot create, modify, or delete events</li>
          <li>Event data (titles, times, attendees, descriptions) is fetched directly from Google's API to your device</li>
          <li>Calendar data is held in memory only and is never written to disk or sent to any third-party server</li>
          <li>OAuth tokens are encrypted using macOS Keychain (via Electron safeStorage) and stored locally</li>
          <li>You can disconnect Google Calendar at any time from Settings, which revokes access and deletes stored tokens</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Google user data: collection, use, and protection</h2>
        <p>This section describes how StenoAI handles data received from Google APIs, in compliance with the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>.</p>

        <h3>Data accessed</h3>
        <p>When you connect Google Calendar, StenoAI accesses the following Google user data via the <code>calendar.readonly</code> scope:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Calendar event titles and descriptions</li>
          <li>Event start and end times</li>
          <li>Attendee names and email addresses</li>
          <li>Event metadata (location, recurrence, status)</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Data usage</h3>
        <p>Google Calendar data is used solely to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Display your upcoming meetings within the StenoAI interface so you can quickly start recording a session</li>
          <li>Auto-populate meeting names and attendee lists for your transcription sessions</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Google user data is never used for advertising, profiling, or any purpose unrelated to the app's core meeting-transcription functionality.</p>
        <p><strong>Google Workspace APIs are not used to develop, improve, or train generalized AI and/or ML models.</strong> Data retrieved from Google Workspace APIs (including Google Calendar) is used solely for the user-facing features described above and is never used as training data, fine-tuning data, or input to any AI/ML model, generalized or otherwise.</p>

        <h3>Data sharing</h3>
        <p>StenoAI does <strong>not</strong> share, sell, or transfer Google user data to any third party. Calendar data stays entirely on your device and is never sent to StenoAI servers, analytics services, or any other external service.</p>

        <h3>Data storage and protection</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Calendar event data is held <strong>in memory only</strong> while the app is running. It is never persisted to disk.</li>
          <li>OAuth refresh and access tokens are encrypted at rest using <strong>macOS Keychain</strong> via Electron's safeStorage API, which provides OS-level encryption tied to your user account.</li>
          <li>All communication with Google APIs occurs over HTTPS/TLS.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Data retention and deletion</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Calendar event data is not retained; it exists only in application memory and is discarded when the app is closed or when you navigate away from the calendar view.</li>
          <li>OAuth tokens are retained locally until you disconnect Google Calendar.</li>
          <li><strong>To delete all Google data:</strong> Open StenoAI Settings and click "Disconnect Google Calendar." This immediately revokes the OAuth token with Google and deletes all stored credentials from your device.</li>
          <li>Uninstalling StenoAI also removes all locally stored tokens and data.</li>
          <li>You can also revoke access at any time from your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions page</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Analytics (optional)</h2>
        <p>StenoAI includes optional, privacy-safe analytics via PostHog to help improve the product. This can be disabled in Settings. When enabled, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Anonymous usage events (e.g., "recording started", "summary generated")</li>
          <li>Duration buckets (e.g., "5-15 minutes"), never exact durations</li>
          <li>App version and platform information</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We never collect or transmit: audio content, transcript text, summary content, file paths, meeting names, or any personally identifiable information.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>StenoAI connects to the internet only for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Google Calendar API (if connected by you)</li>
          <li>PostHog analytics (enabled by default; can be disabled in Settings)</li>
          <li>Checking for app updates via GitHub</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>For privacy-related questions, open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/stenolabs/stenoai">GitHub</a> or reach out on <a href="https://discord.gg/DZ6vcQnxxu">Discord</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
